The evidence is consistent: a single fault, a payment pod replacement, that propagated along the checkout path. Final answer:

```json
{
  "root_causes": [
    {
      "service": "payment",
      "fault_kind": "pod_failure",
      "evidence": [
        {"kind": "metric", "sql": "SELECT 'abnormal' AS period, attr_k8s_pod_name, count(*) AS samples, min(time) AS first_seen, max(time) AS last_seen FROM abnormal_metrics WHERE service_name='payment' AND metric='k8s.pod.uptime' GROUP BY 1,2 UNION ALL SELECT 'normal', attr_k8s_pod_name, count(*), min(time), max(time) FROM normal_metrics WHERE service_name='payment' AND metric='k8s.pod.uptime' GROUP BY 1,2", "claim": "Payment's pod was replaced: normal period ran payment-6bdd596cf7-tm4zx, abnormal period runs a new pod -qcrbb."},
        {"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT time, span_name, duration/1e6 AS ms, attr_k8s_pod_name FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name='payment' AND span_name LIKE '%PaymentService/Charge' ORDER BY time", "claim": "Payment Charge spans in the abnormal window: a 14.8 ms first call after a dns.lookup and tcp.connect, then sub-millisecond calls."},
        {"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT service_name, time_bucket(INTERVAL 30 SECOND, time) AS b, count(*) AS spans FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name IN ('payment','checkout') GROUP BY 1,2 ORDER BY 2,1", "claim": "Payment and checkout spans drop to zero for about a minute (around 11:09:30 to 11:10:30) before payment traffic resumes."}
      ]
    }
  ],
  "propagation": [
    {"from": "payment", "to": "checkout", "evidence": [{"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT service_name, span_name, duration/1e6 AS ms FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name='checkout' AND span_name='oteldemo.PaymentService/Charge' ORDER BY time", "claim": "Checkout's client Charge calls to payment take 23 ms in the abnormal window, against about 0.6 ms in normal."}]},
    {"from": "checkout", "to": "frontend", "evidence": [{"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT service_name, span_name, approx_quantile(duration,0.95)/1e6 AS p95_ms FROM abnormal_traces WHERE span_name IN ('oteldemo.CheckoutService/PlaceOrder','POST /api/checkout') GROUP BY 1,2", "claim": "Checkout PlaceOrder and frontend POST /api/checkout p95 rise to about 45 ms and 54 ms, with no HTTP errors."}]},
    {"from": "frontend", "to": "frontend-proxy", "evidence": [{"kind": "trace", "sql": "SELECT service_name, span_name, approx_quantile(duration,0.95)/1e6 AS p95_ms FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name='frontend-proxy' AND span_name='ingress' GROUP BY 1,2", "claim": "Frontend-proxy ingress spans carry the slower checkout requests; its p95 stays near 16 ms, with status codes unchanged."}]}
  ]
}
```

